## GML Examples
# DEPT Trends — GML Examples

Reference cards showing how the DEPT Trends editorial style translates to GML. The 3 pillars: DISPLAY-scale typography, image-layout="behind", aggressive background-color alternation. The signature move: accent-italic-word in DISPLAY text. Sentence case throughout. Zero questions on dividers.

## Title splash card (accent background + DISPLAY + accent italic word)

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" background-color="#00FF00">
  <DIV class="body">
    <P><B>2025 trends report</B></P>
    <DISPLAY size="lg">The future belongs to the <I><SPAN text-color="#000000">impatient</SPAN></I></DISPLAY>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Section divider with smart layout (DISPLAY + accent italic word + solidBoxes)

Divider cards use smart layouts for structured items — NOT plain UL. The smart-layout variant is consistent across the entire deck (one variant only).

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank">
  <DIV class="body">
    <DISPLAY size="lg">The small becomes <I><SPAN text-color="accent1">big</SPAN></I></DISPLAY>
    <SMART-LAYOUT variant="solidBoxes" cellSize="10">
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>AI transformation gets fast and furious</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>AI is the democratizer — what's your differentiator?</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>AdTech prepares for personalization at scale</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
    </SMART-LAYOUT>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Section divider with outlineBoxes variant

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank">
  <DIV class="body">
    <DISPLAY size="lg">Creativity in the age of <I><SPAN text-color="accent2">automation</SPAN></I></DISPLAY>
    <SMART-LAYOUT variant="outlineBoxes" cellSize="10">
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>The new creative toolkit</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>Human taste as competitive advantage</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
        <H4><B>Brand voice in an AI-generated world</B></H4>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
    </SMART-LAYOUT>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Article opener (image-layout="behind" + DISPLAY + accent italic word)

```html
<SECTION image-layout="behind">
  <DIV class="body">
    <DISPLAY size="md"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">AI transformation gets </SPAN><I><SPAN text-color="accent1">fast</SPAN></I><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF"> and </SPAN><I><SPAN text-color="accent1">furious</SPAN></I></DISPLAY>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Statement + content card (punchy H2 headline + image-layout="right" + body text)

CRITICAL: Content card headlines use H2, NEVER H1. Max 8-10 words. Punchy claims, not full sentence paragraphs. H1 is only for display-level text on openers/dividers.

```html
<SECTION image-layout="right">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H2><B>AI adoption speed separates winners from losers</B></H2>
    <P>AI advancements are accelerating, transforming industries faster than previous technological shifts. Are you stuck in an AI rut?</P>
    <P>Your competitors are probably <SPAN text-color="accent1">ahead of you</SPAN>.</P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Quote card (image-layout="behind" + large DISPLAY quote + attribution)

IMPORTANT: Quote cards MUST use DISPLAY (not BLOCKQUOTE or H1) for the headline quote. DISPLAY creates the massive, dramatic text treatment that defines this card type. Use size="md" or "lg".

```html
<SECTION image-layout="behind">
  <DIV class="body">
    <DISPLAY size="md"><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">"This moment in computing history will reshape many enterprise businesses."</SPAN></DISPLAY>
    <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">"Organizations need to have a strong grasp on how rapid the innovation cycle will be with AI transformation."</SPAN></P>
    <P><B><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Jamie Allan</SPAN></B></P>
    <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Director, AdTech & Digital Marketing Industries, NVIDIA</SPAN></P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Analytical spread with varied column headers

Column headers vary per card — NEVER default to "What's ahead" / "Where to start". Each analytical card picks headers matching its content.

### Example 1: "Key implications" / "Next steps"

```html
<SECTION image-layout="right">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent1">Key implications</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>As AI continues democratizing technology, the challenge shifts from access to differentiation.</P>
        <P>Focus on what sets you apart — unique data and creative storytelling.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent1">Next steps</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>Use AI to scale operations while prioritizing proprietary data as a differentiator.</P>
        <P>Keep storytelling at the heart of your strategy — emotional intelligence drives brand identity.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

### Example 2: "The opportunity" / "The challenge"

```html
<SECTION image-layout="right">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent2">The opportunity</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>Real-time personalization can drive 3x engagement over static content. Brands that invest in dynamic content infrastructure will capture outsized attention share.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent2">The challenge</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>Privacy regulations and cookie deprecation make targeting harder. First-party data strategies are no longer optional — they're the foundation.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

### Example 3: "For enterprises" / "For startups"

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[50,50]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent1">For enterprises</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>Build dedicated AI operations teams. Invest in data pipelines that feed agent systems. Treat AI agents as infrastructure, not experiments.</P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><B><SPAN text-color="accent1">For startups</SPAN></B></H4>
        <P>Move fast on agent integration. Your agility is an advantage — deploy agents in customer-facing roles where incumbents move slowly.</P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Content card with accent sub-header and highlighted phrases (H2 headline)

```html
<SECTION image-layout="right">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H2><B>Brand differentiation depends on <I><SPAN text-color="accent1">human creativity</SPAN></I></B></H2>
    <P>AI tools are no longer a competitive advantage — they're infrastructure that helps you scale and <SPAN text-color="accent1">unlock data-driven insights</SPAN>.</P>
    <P>Every brand can now access high-quality outputs once exclusive to industry leaders.</P>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Data/stat card with horizontal stats

Stats MUST render horizontally (side by side), never stacked vertically. Use orientation="horizontal" on the stats smart-layout.

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank">
  <DIV class="body">
    <H2><B>Consumers already shop with AI</B></H2>
    <SMART-LAYOUT variant="stats" cellSize="12" orientation="horizontal">
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="86%">
        <P>want AI to research products</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="79%">
        <P>want AI to find deals</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
      <SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM number="82%">
        <P>interested in AI customer service</P>
      </SMART-LAYOUT-ITEM>
    </SMART-LAYOUT>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

## Showcase card (dark background + 3-col with descriptions)

```html
<SECTION image-layout="blank" background-color="#111111">
  <DIV class="body">
    <COLUMNS colWidths="[33,33,34]">
      <DIV>
        <H4><SPAN text-color="accent1">The ever-present shop assistant</SPAN></H4>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Users can search for "furniture for my college dorm room" and find results smoothly integrated into the current layout.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><SPAN text-color="accent1">The commerce navigator</SPAN></H4>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Users can go straight to the page they're looking for — even if they don't quite know what page that is.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
      <DIV>
        <H4><SPAN text-color="accent1">The virtual visualizer</SPAN></H4>
        <P><SPAN text-color="#FFFFFF">Imagine adding furniture to virtual spaces while shopping online, placing items into customizable rooms as you browse.</SPAN></P>
      </DIV>
    </COLUMNS>
  </DIV>
</SECTION>
```

